  <!-- About Section -->
  <!-- Contained 2026-08-14 (RED-1): seven of nine claims fail or need a ruling; surgical removal is not available. BARRED: "$246 million in patient savings" (§6 — arithmetic on the void 400,000-case multiplicand; no cumulative savings figure exists anywhere in the 36-document corpus; named in the removal worklist); "one of the first nationwide diagnostic imaging networks" (D3 — narrowed forms including this exact string were considered and REJECTED); "more than 1,200 imaging centers" (rule 18 third form — approved compact is "1,200+ centers", canonical is "1,228 contracted imaging facilities in 43 states, April 2002" — and no April 2002 anchor, so an AnciCare-era count reads as a present USRad network); "After decades" (#27 tenure (a) — AnciCare ran eight years, 1994-2002, in unsigned prose). REMOVING THE BARRED MATERIAL LEAVES A SECTION THAT IS WORSE THAN BROKEN: the H2 asserts "Proven" with every number gone, and the residual "built on the foundation of a diagnostic imaging network" — no scale, no date, no ended-in-2002 marker — reads as a network USRad has NOW. That is a rule 26 failure PRODUCED BY DELETION, the outcome G-1 warned of: no softened restatement, no smaller claim in the same slot. #22 predicted it in terms: find-and-replace would leave headings with nothing under them. COMPONENT PRESERVED, NOT DELETED — the section's shape is the right vessel and §4a holds a verified set (1,228 facilities/43 states April 2002, $60M+ paid 1994-2001, founded 1994, acquired by CorVel Corporation NASDAQ: CRVL May 2002, Inc. 500 #210) for a later credibility rebuild under #22's two-pass discipline. The "Read the full story →" CTA to /about goes with it; /about is unremediated and the homepage promotes what it links to. ⛔ CONTAINING / DOES NOT CLOSE §6 — $246M survives at blog/the-scan-that-never-happens:306. -->
  <!-- <AboutSection /> -->

  <!-- Blog Preview Section -->
  <BlogPreviewSection />
</CarbonLayout>

<style>
  /* CSS-only scroll animations - no JS dependency */
  .animate-on-scroll {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(20px);
    animation: fadeInUp 0.6s ease-out forwards;
  }

  @keyframes fadeInUp {
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }

  /* Optional: Use Intersection Observer via CSS if you want scroll-triggered animations */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .animate-on-scroll {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>
